+            // same shape read back from ODP (whose frame was grown on save) did not. Let the paper grow sideways and keep the
+            // frame as it is. A frame with a left, centre or right horizontal adjust is placed by the adjust below. A block frame
+            // (the adjust is the paragraphs' own) is let grow only when every paragraph names its alignment and they agree
+            // (left, centre or right): that alignment then becomes the frame's adjust, so the line is centred on the frame, or
+            // ends at its right edge, as in PowerPoint. Anything else keeps the old limit.
+            if (!bVerticalWriting && !rSdrBlockTextPrimitive.getWordWrap() && IsAutoGrowWidth())
+            {
